== choice_1
   Haha, those petty villagers, still thinking of getting those missing persons back? Missing for a month or two days, what's the difference? They all bacame<color=red>fertilizer</color> after all. #Layout:Left
    ->END
  
== choice_2
    Honest and Clean? Hahaha! The world is full of hypocrites. #Layout:Left
    ->END

== choice_3
   It's that coward's saber. He had it for half a lifetime, and finally sees the blood. #Layout:Left
    ->END
    
== choice_4
  It's the waste of the elixir by that dumbass. That coward wouldn't dare to get into the flower room every time, it got to be me who went in. 
  He wouldn't dare to go into the flower room, because he was scared of those medicine puppets. Such a hypocrite. #Layout:Left #CE:ED_9
    ->END

== choice_5
I don't know where that damn master got the seeds of the flowers of Wangchuan. It resonated with me somehow.  #Layout:Left #CE:ED_11
    ->END
    
== choice_6
Pretty, isn't it? Red like blood, petals are like the fire. Never know you have these beautiful things in the netherworld. #Layout:Left
    ->END
    
== choice_7
Wangyou elixir, haha! That damn master said it can cure disease, but in fact he uses it to color=red>extend his own life</color>. The more he eats, the harder to leave it, funny!#Layout:Left #CE:ED_14
    ->END
    
== choice_8
That damn master's writing is less useful than toilet paper. Except for the flower of Wangchuan, the rest is rubbish. Bur he wrote it with such en effort. #Layout:Left #CE:ED_16
    ->END
    
== choice_9
The flower of Wangchuan is so magical. With living people's flesh, the seeds can quickly grow<color=red>bulbs and then bloom</color>; But when the poeple die, <color=red>the bulbs and flowers all die out</color>, those bulbs turn into seeds hard as stones, as if they are waiting for the next round of life and death. #Layout:Left #CE:ED_17
    ->END
->END
